questions.q:
An inorganic compound $\mathrm{W}$ undergoes the following reactions:
$
\begin{gathered}
W+\dfrac{\mathrm{Na}_2 \mathrm{CO}_3}{\mathrm{O}_2 / \text { heat }} \rightarrow X+\dfrac{\mathrm{H}^{+}}{} \rightarrow Y_{(s)} \\
Y(a q)+\mathrm{KCl}(\mathrm{aq}) \rightarrow Z_{(S)}
\end{gathered}
$
Z appears in the form of orange crystals and is used as an oxidising agent in acid medium. Identify the compound W.

