The Rydberg formula for the wave number $ ar{
u}$ of a transition in the hydrogen spectrum is given by $ ar{
u} = R_H Z^2 \left( \dfrac{1}{n_1^2} - \dfrac{1}{n_2^2} ight)$, where $R_H = 109677 	ext{ cm}^{-1}$ and $Z = 1$ for hydrogen.<br><br>For the Balmer series, the transition ends at $n_1 = 2$. The longest wavelength transition corresponds to the smallest energy difference, which occurs for the transition from the nearest higher energy level, $n_2 = 3$.<br><br>Substituting these values into the formula:<br><br>$ ar{
